      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1" ana="#tr.print">The framed manuscript page number [ⲕⲇ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke. Line 1 is in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲧ. Measured overline over ⲡⲛⲁ (1105–1150): ⲡ 84 %, ⲛ 100 %, ⲁ 58 %; not over ⲙ.</p>
        <p n="9" ana="#tr.bracket">The bracket before the last dots is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end. So also ll. 12, 13, 17, 26 and 33.</p>
        <p n="12" ana="#tr.print">Measured overline over ⲡⲛⲁ of ⲡⲡⲛⲁ (924–970): it covers the second ⲡ, ⲛ and ⲁ, not the first ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="15" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke in [ⲣⲙⲙ] (563–576): over the first ⲙ only.</p>
        <p n="16" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲧ inside the restoration.</p>
        <p n="18" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲧ begins ⲧⲥⲟⲫⲓⲁ after the blank. The dot under ⲡ of ⲙⲡⲓⲱⲧ is faint (below the detector's area threshold) but visible at 5×.</p>
        <p n="19" ana="#tr.layout">A wide blank, not marked by the editors, stands before the enlarged ⲧ of ⲧϭⲁⲙ.</p>
        <p n="21" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="22" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲧ begins ⲧⲉⲩⲇⲁⲓⲙⲟⲛⲓⲁ. Measured stroke over ⲙⲛ (635–655): ⲙ 52 %, ⲛ 57 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="24" ana="#tr.print">ⲡⲛⲁ is printed without an overline here (measured: no stroke over 539–594), unlike ll. 1 and 12.</p>
        <p n="28" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ. The edition opens a bracket after ⲟⲩⲥⲟⲫ and closes it at the line end.</p>
        <p n="31" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲧ begins ⲧⲥⲟⲫⲓⲁ after the blank.</p>
      </div>
